WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:06.560
When running a loop, you may need to change&nbsp;
the code that displays for a loop iteration,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.200
as we have seen with the break or continue&nbsp;
statement. Still, as you build an app, you may not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.560
know what code is needed in a certain spot and may&nbsp;
want to leave a placeholder for possible code to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:23.640
add later. The Pass keyword is that placeholder.&nbsp;
Pass is unlike the break or continue keywords,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:29.120
as it does not break out of a loop or pause a&nbsp;
loop. To see how pass works in the context of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:38.880
a loop, I will, in this 225-pass file, replace the&nbsp;
print statement, on line 5, with a pass statement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:45.320
as the game testers are not sure if the message&nbsp;
in place is correct. I will leave the continue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:54.160
statement in so that the print statement on line 7&nbsp;
runs for the other coins. Let’s run this code. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:01:01.640
expected, the coins that are not platinum printed.&nbsp;
Pass is valuable because it allows one to build&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:06.440
parts of code while waiting for information and&nbsp;
thus continue to structure code without waiting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:12.160
unnecessarily, saving overall time in building&nbsp;
apps. After all, having a framework and filling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:19.280
in details is much more efficient than waiting&nbsp;
on information before even building a framework.

